# Neo Delay parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoDelay
namespace NeoBuzz.Delay
class NeoDelayMachine
summary Tempo-synced stereo delay: stereo, ping-pong or cross-feedback lines, the time free in ms or synced to the song (straight, dotted, triplet), feedback to ±99 % through a high-pass, a low-pass and a tape-style saturator in the loop, a little modulation, ducking by the input, width, mix and output. Time changes glide (small ones bend the pitch, large ones crossfade); the line can't run away at any setting. Zero latency; at Mix 0 % it passes the input bit for bit. Use it for echoes and space in a mix (a send at 100 % wet, or an insert), dub and tape echoes, ping-pong throws, slapback and doubling.

group Time
Mode      "Mode"           0 2     0     enum Stereo Ping-pong Cross     | Stereo: each channel echoes on its own side; Ping-pong: the input (mono) enters the left line and the echoes bounce left, right, left; Cross: each side's echo feeds the other side's line, so a left sound's echoes bounce and a centred one stays centred
    how Chooses how the echoes travel: each side on its own, bouncing left and right, or crossing from side to side.
    sound Stereo keeps a wide source wide, Ping-pong throws each echo across the picture, and Cross bounces off-centre sounds while centred ones stay put.
Sync      "Sync"           0 8     4     enum Free 1/64 1/32 1/16 1/8 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars | The delay as a note value of the song's tempo (Feel makes it dotted or triplet); Free: Time in ms
    how Locks the delay time to a note length of the song tempo, or leaves it free in milliseconds.
    sound Synced echoes sit in the groove of the track; Free lets the repeats drift against it for slapback or loose tape echoes.
Feel      "Feel"           0 2     1     enum Straight Dotted Triplet    | With Sync: the note value straight, dotted (× 1.5) or triplet (× 2/3)
    how Makes the synced note straight, dotted (one and a half times as long) or a triplet (two thirds as long).
    sound Dotted echoes give a skipping, rolling pattern and triplets a swung one, while straight ones stay square.
Time      "Time"           0 10000 6959  time 0.001 5                   | The delay when Sync is Free, 1 ms – 5 s
    how Sets the delay from 1 ms to 5 s when Sync is Free.
    sound Very short times thicken or double the sound, around 100 ms gives slapback, and long times give distinct echoes.
Offset    "Offset"         0 1500  500   lin -50 100 % 1                | The right line's time against the left's: −50 % half as long, +100 % twice as long (0: the same)
    how Makes the right line shorter or longer than the left, from minus 50 % to plus 100 %.
    sound An offset spreads the repeats into a wide, uneven pattern; zero keeps both sides in step.
group Feedback
Feedback  "Feedback"       0 1980  1340  lin -99 99 % 1                 | Echoes fed back into the line; negative inverts each repeat. Bounded to ±99 %, and the line saturates softly, so it can't run away
    how Sets how much of the echo returns into the line, from minus 99 % to plus 99 %; negative values flip each repeat.
    sound Low values give one or two repeats, high values a long fading trail, and negative values a hollower, more nasal repeat.
LowCut    "Low cut"        0 1000  291   freq 20 5000                   | High-pass in the loop, 12 dB/oct (Butterworth), −3 dB here: each repeat thinner. At its bottom (20 Hz) it is off
    how Removes low frequencies from each repeat in the loop, from 20 Hz to 5 kHz.
    sound Raising it keeps the repeats thin and clear of the bass, so long trails do not build up mud.
HighCut   "High cut"       0 1000  801   freq 200 20000                 | Low-pass in the loop, 12 dB/oct (two real poles), −3 dB here: each repeat darker. At its top (20 kHz) it is open
    how Rolls off high frequencies of each repeat in the loop, from 200 Hz to 20 kHz.
    sound Lowering it makes every repeat darker than the last, like an old tape or analogue echo.
Drive     "Drive"          0 240   0     lin 0 24 dB 1                  | Tape-style saturation of what enters the line: above −Drive dBFS the echoes bend softly towards 6 dB over it (0 dB: clean up to full scale)
    how Pushes what enters the line into soft saturation by up to 24 dB.
    sound A little adds warmth and glue to the repeats; a lot makes them crunchy and compressed.
group Motion
ModDepth  "Mod depth"      0 1000  0     lin 0 5 ms 2                   | Tape wow: the delay moves this much either way (the right line a quarter cycle on), at most half the delay
    how Sets how far the delay time wobbles, from 0 to 5 ms.
    sound Small amounts add a gentle tape-like waver, larger ones a seasick pitch warble on the repeats.
ModRate   "Mod rate"       0 1000  500   freq 0.05 5                    | Speed of the wow
    how Sets the speed of the wobble, from 0.05 to 5 Hz.
    sound Slow rates sound like worn tape drifting; faster rates turn into a chorus-like shimmer.
group Ducking
Duck      "Duck"           0 400   0     lin 0 40 dB 1                  | How far the echoes are turned down while the input plays above Duck threshold (0: off)
    how Turns the echoes down by up to 40 dB while the input is playing.
    sound Ducking keeps the echoes out of the way of the dry sound and lets them bloom in the gaps.
DuckThresh "Duck threshold" 0 600  300   lin -60 0 dB 1                 | Input level (peak) where ducking reaches its full depth; it fades in over the 12 dB below
    how Sets the input level, from -60 to 0 dB, at which ducking reaches its full depth.
    sound A low threshold ducks on quiet playing too; a high one only reacts to loud notes.
DuckRelease "Duck release" 0 1000  548   time 0.02 2                    | How fast the echoes come back once the input falls (time constant)
    how Sets how quickly the echoes return after the input stops, from 20 ms to 2 s.
    sound Short times bring the echoes back at once, long ones let them swell in slowly after each phrase.
group Output
Width     "Width"          0 200   100   lin 0 200 % 0                  | The echoes' side signal × width: 0 % mono echoes, 100 % as they are, 200 % twice as wide
    how Scales the stereo width of the echoes from 0 to 200 %.
    sound At 0 % the echoes are mono and focused, and past 100 % they spread wider than the source.
Mix       "Mix"            0 1000  300   pct                            | Dry against wet (a crossfade): 100 % for a send
    how Blends the dry sound with the echoes from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Use a low value as an insert for subtle depth, or 100 % when the delay sits on a send.
Output    "Output"         0 240   120   db -12 12                      | Output gain, −12 … +12 dB in 0.1 dB steps
    how Sets the output gain, from minus 12 to plus 12 dB.
    sound Use it to match the level of the delay to the track once the settings are right.
